[statement]
A later name's dependency that only a provider at no version without a
priority could answer steers no earlier choice: `top` needs `so:x`, then
`w`; `app`, the one candidate for `w`, needs `so:y`, which only `old`
provides, at no version and without a priority, and `old` cannot be
installed beside `new`, the best candidate for `so:x`. `so:x` keeps
`new`, and apk refuses `so:y`. With a priority on `old`, `app`'s
dependency steers `so:x` to `old`, and apk installs `old`, `app` and
`top`.

[repository]
P:top
V:1
D:so:x w

P:app
V:1
D:so:y
p:w=1

P:new
V:1
p:so:x=3

P:old
V:1
p:so:x so:y

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   so:y (virtual):
|     note: please select one of the 'provided by'
|           packages explicitly
|     provided by: old
|     required by: app-1[so:y]
refused
